WEBVTT

00:28.063 --> 00:33.039
Umm, I'd like to thank you all for coming
to this eve of the Founder's Festival.

00:34.089 --> 00:38.064
My name is Rimuru. I have recently
been appointed a Demon Lord.

00:38.064 --> 00:41.004
Today I'd like to set
the difficult topics aside

00:41.004 --> 00:45.009
and hope that all of you here
will enjoy our nation's dishes.

00:45.009 --> 00:48.032
I was never one for long speeches,

00:48.032 --> 00:50.041
so let's get this started
without further ado.

00:50.041 --> 00:53.003
Cheers!

01:57.018 --> 02:01.023
THAT TIME I GOT REINCARNATED AS A SLIME

02:23.075 --> 02:27.088
EPISODE 67: THE EVE OF THE FESTIVAL

02:28.059 --> 02:31.003
These are good! I expect no less
from Shuna and Mr. Yoshida.

02:31.092 --> 02:35.006
Our guests seem to be enjoying
themselves, so that's a relief.

02:41.082 --> 02:43.056
What's that, Rimuru?

02:43.056 --> 02:45.002
Oh, it's starting.

02:48.036 --> 02:50.015
What kind of fish is that?

02:50.015 --> 02:52.034
What a fearsome look.

03:13.024 --> 03:15.072
Wow! They look tasty!

03:15.072 --> 03:16.068
Ah, but...

03:17.059 --> 03:20.013
Nobody's taking them...

03:20.013 --> 03:24.035
We have no customs of eating
raw fish in this world, after all.

03:24.035 --> 03:27.027
Sorry man, I'll have to pass on this one.

03:27.027 --> 03:30.052
So they think this is some
low-grade garbage food, huh.

03:30.052 --> 03:31.023
All right.

03:35.019 --> 03:36.032
I'll take one.

03:36.007 --> 03:39.007
Oh, by all means...

03:39.007 --> 03:40.007
Enjoy!

03:50.033 --> 03:52.042
This is the best, Hakuro!

03:52.042 --> 03:53.067
That it is, I'm sure!

03:53.067 --> 03:58.055
I was concerned such fine fish
may not last for long,

03:58.055 --> 04:01.005
but it seems I wouldn't have
to worry about that.

04:01.045 --> 04:04.031
I'll look forward to eating
these after this, no doubt!

04:05.057 --> 04:09.006
Would you make me a piece of tuna underbelly
without the wasabi, please?

04:10.081 --> 04:12.044
What are you, a child?

04:12.044 --> 04:13.009
Oh, shut it.

04:13.009 --> 04:16.065
I don't like the way
it stings in my nose.

04:16.065 --> 04:17.082
Also...

04:18.002 --> 04:20.002
A little more variety would be nice.

04:20.002 --> 04:21.099
You sure are asking for a lot.

04:21.099 --> 04:25.029
A real connoisseur knows how to enjoy
the flavor of the wasabi, you know?

04:25.029 --> 04:27.000
Who cares?

04:27.000 --> 04:28.052
What's that even matter?

04:28.052 --> 04:30.008
If it tastes good, it tastes good.

04:30.008 --> 04:31.055
Kept you waiting!

04:38.059 --> 04:40.051
This is really the best.

04:41.001 --> 04:44.085
It pisses me off,
but I respect you for this, Rimuru.

04:45.043 --> 04:48.073
I'll have one too, then.

04:48.073 --> 04:52.048
Oh, and I'm not a kid,
so I'll have mine with wasabi.

04:56.023 --> 04:59.036
Whoa! It just melted in my mouth!

04:59.036 --> 05:04.062
Man, it's kinda touching how I can
eat sushi this good in this world.

05:05.033 --> 05:08.029
It's really different
from a freshwater fish.

05:08.029 --> 05:11.025
I asked Free Guild for a fish like this,
but they turned me down.

05:11.025 --> 05:14.019
And I can't get them teleported
with magic, so I had given up on it.

05:14.019 --> 05:16.074
But now I have more things
to look forward to in life.

05:16.074 --> 05:18.038
There's nothing
we can do about that.

05:18.038 --> 05:22.043
The northern seas are too dangerous
with all the giant sea creatures.

05:22.084 --> 05:26.001
And the south is too far away
to transport them all the way here.

05:26.001 --> 05:30.031
You can't make a profit off just shipping
the seafood from the inland waters.

05:31.002 --> 05:35.044
I knew it. There are still a lot of issues
with transportation in this world.

05:35.044 --> 05:37.002
All according to plan.

05:37.041 --> 05:41.052
If our guests learn the existence of
delights exclusive to Tempest...

05:42.045 --> 05:43.045
Sir Rimuru.

05:44.028 --> 05:46.075
May we have some of those as well?

05:49.004 --> 05:50.037
Yes, of course.

05:54.029 --> 05:55.046
Excellent as always.

05:55.046 --> 05:57.046
Mmmh! This is good!

05:57.091 --> 06:00.097
I had no idea that monster fish
could be this delicious.

06:00.097 --> 06:04.097
I thought all you can do
with fish is to grill them.

06:05.055 --> 06:08.001
Hey, if it tastes good,
there's nothing wrong with it.

06:09.068 --> 06:11.089
Me too! I'll have that as well!

06:11.089 --> 06:13.031
So am I!

06:13.031 --> 06:14.004
Me too!

06:16.098 --> 06:18.015
Urgent news!

06:18.015 --> 06:20.015
What's the matter?
Did something happen?

06:20.015 --> 06:24.006
A large flying object
has flown into the town!

06:24.057 --> 06:26.047
A flying object?

06:30.054 --> 06:31.066
Reporting!

06:31.066 --> 06:36.025
S-Sorcerous Dynasty of Thalion's
guardian dragon has appeared!

06:36.092 --> 06:38.029
It's an emergency!

06:38.029 --> 06:42.059
Emperor Elmesia El-Ru Thalion herself
has set foot upon this land!

06:42.059 --> 06:47.035
Her Excellency Elmesia and her entourage
are walking toward this reception hall!

06:48.001 --> 06:49.076
Oh, that's a relief.

06:49.076 --> 06:51.035
I was wondering what was up.

06:51.085 --> 06:55.048
You're just as thoughtless
and ignorant as ever, eh?

06:55.048 --> 07:00.011
This kind of reaction is to be expected
if that Emperor Elmesia left her borders.

07:00.057 --> 07:01.086
What do you mean by that?

07:02.061 --> 07:05.037
The Sorcerous Dynasty of Thalion
is a large nation.

07:05.037 --> 07:09.045
They boast military prowess
on par with Dwargon's,

07:09.045 --> 07:13.083
and is an entirely independent nation,
not involved with the Council of the West.

07:14.041 --> 07:17.025
And as their name "Dynasty" implies,

07:17.025 --> 07:20.017
it is a federation of
thirteen distinct kingdoms.

07:21.000 --> 07:24.038
The Emperor Elmesia is hailed
as a descendant of divinity

07:24.038 --> 07:28.055
and holds immense power that allows her
to declare herself the Heavenly Emperor.

07:29.018 --> 07:31.018
Dwargon has existed for a thousand years.

07:31.018 --> 07:34.093
And Thalion is said to have existed
for over two thousand years.

07:36.031 --> 07:40.019
That means not even I can
raise my head high against her.

07:40.019 --> 07:45.044
Humans who have much shorter life spans
would never have the chance to meet her.

07:46.007 --> 07:47.053
I see.

07:47.053 --> 07:50.024
I meant to invite only Archduke Erald,

07:50.024 --> 07:53.007
but I ended up landing
someone much bigger, huh.

07:53.007 --> 07:56.049
Oh, seems like they've finally arrived.

07:57.096 --> 08:00.004
Don't let your guard down, Rimuru.

08:01.061 --> 08:05.005
Think of her as the sliest
old fox you'll ever see.

08:10.047 --> 08:13.006
I have accepted your kind invitation.

08:14.001 --> 08:15.098
It gladdened me.

08:19.048 --> 08:22.064
Likewise, it is an honor to meet you...

08:23.057 --> 08:27.049
Report. Detecting mental interference.
Blocked.

08:27.092 --> 08:32.028
This is likely not an attack,
but an effect of her Heroic Aura skill leaking.

08:32.028 --> 08:37.005
Oh crap! This lady's Heroic Aura is on
a whole 'nother level compared to Gazel's!

08:37.085 --> 08:40.083
Looks like it'd be better
not to get on her bad side.

08:40.083 --> 08:44.005
I'd love it if you could enjoy
your visit here this evening!

08:44.084 --> 08:46.009
Yes.

08:46.009 --> 08:49.001
I do look forward to
this festival tomorrow,

08:49.001 --> 08:51.051
and I hope they prove
to be eminently enjoyable.

08:52.026 --> 08:53.033
Also...

08:54.018 --> 08:58.002
It doesn't have to be today,
but could you make time for me?

08:58.044 --> 09:02.027
There's something I wanna discuss
with you in a more relaxed environment.

09:03.098 --> 09:06.078
All right. I'll let you know
once we figure out the time.

09:12.099 --> 09:15.028
Man, I'm beat.

09:15.028 --> 09:18.023
You were so close to getting
swallowed up by her, weren't you?

09:18.023 --> 09:20.079
If you hadn't kept yourself sharp,
that old hag would've...

09:24.029 --> 09:27.084
Seems like elves have good hearing.
I should watch out, too.

09:27.084 --> 09:29.042
Great Rimuru!

09:29.081 --> 09:32.097
Oh, Mjöllmile!
How's the preparation going?

09:32.097 --> 09:34.093
It's all going well!

09:35.029 --> 09:38.031
The merchants had a good
first impression of the town

09:38.031 --> 09:41.048
and I think we can build good ties
with them from now on.

09:41.048 --> 09:43.019
Sounds like it's all good on your side.

09:43.019 --> 09:44.081
Yes, sir.
It's all in good hands.

09:44.081 --> 09:48.061
But... Well... Umm...

09:48.061 --> 09:49.086
It's fine.

09:49.086 --> 09:51.057
Hm? What is it?

09:51.057 --> 09:54.074
Hm, I hope it's just my imagination,

09:54.074 --> 09:57.083
but I am recognizing rather
few of the tradespeople working here

09:57.083 --> 10:00.083
alongside the large merchants
I have close ties to.

10:00.083 --> 10:05.046
It caught my attention,
so I decided to look into it...

10:06.084 --> 10:09.046
But well, there's no problem to speak of.

10:09.046 --> 10:15.097
Perhaps being given such a large task
has made me a tad high-strung.

10:15.097 --> 10:17.097
Well then, if you excuse me.

10:17.097 --> 10:19.047
You're not going to stay and eat?

10:19.047 --> 10:24.023
I still have to prepare for tomorrow's
battle tournament. I can't rest just yet.

10:24.023 --> 10:24.085
See you.

10:24.085 --> 10:27.065
You're such a hard worker, Mjöllmile.

10:28.019 --> 10:30.043
Hey, look.

10:32.007 --> 10:34.028
They're finally here.

10:34.028 --> 10:35.028
Yeah.

10:35.028 --> 10:37.028
They're late, so I got kinda worried.

10:37.069 --> 10:39.062
Sorry, I have to go greet them.

10:39.062 --> 10:41.066
Oh, Milim's here?

10:41.066 --> 10:43.079
Looks like she got all dressed up today.

10:47.021 --> 10:49.005
The Demon Lords have arrived.

10:59.047 --> 11:00.072
With no wasabi.

11:02.031 --> 11:03.081
No wasabi, okay?

11:06.077 --> 11:08.048
Hello, Rimuru!

11:09.004 --> 11:11.023
The day's finally here!

11:11.023 --> 11:15.099
I hope you'll get us food that'll
make Middray knock his socks off!

11:15.099 --> 11:18.007
Yeah, no worries there.

11:18.007 --> 11:21.049
More importantly,
did she get angry with you?

11:21.049 --> 11:22.095
I-It's fine!

11:22.095 --> 11:25.075
I convinced Frey that
I've built up awareness as a ruler

11:25.075 --> 11:29.071
and was out protecting my territory!

11:29.071 --> 11:33.046
You were out protecting a dungeon,
not your territory, though.

11:34.072 --> 11:37.005
And looks like her cover's
been blown...

11:37.072 --> 11:40.072
Thank you for inviting us today.

11:40.072 --> 11:44.039
I apologize for our tardiness.

11:44.039 --> 11:48.056
Lady Milim, our new master,
was missing for quite a long time.

11:48.096 --> 11:52.057
So we didn't have much time
to fit her for her formal wear.

11:54.015 --> 11:58.078
We certainly don't mind it at all,
so please, enjoy yourselves.

11:58.078 --> 12:00.066
Yes, of course.

12:00.066 --> 12:04.095
You were so kind
to build a new city for us,

12:04.095 --> 12:10.054
so I'm so grateful that you also
invited us to this fantastic event.

12:10.054 --> 12:14.042
Well, I hope our food
is to your liking as well.

12:14.042 --> 12:18.005
Oh, right, are there any
ingredients you can't have?

12:18.005 --> 12:20.068
We do have chicken on the menu,
so if it's a proble...

12:22.039 --> 12:23.041
Did you say...

12:24.006 --> 12:25.085
...chicken?

12:25.085 --> 12:29.073
Oh... Oh no!

12:30.073 --> 12:36.036
Sir Rimuru, are you equating us
to mere livestock?

12:36.036 --> 12:38.078
Um, that wasn't my intention...!

12:39.045 --> 12:41.007
A mistake! A slip of the tongue!

12:44.091 --> 12:48.008
Oh man, Sir Rimuru, that was great!

12:48.008 --> 12:51.075
To call Frey a bird!
Now that's just incredible!

12:51.075 --> 12:54.042
Yeah, I could never do that.

12:54.042 --> 12:58.013
Oh, what's so funny, Carrion? Milim?

12:59.055 --> 13:02.064
No, I'm sorry.
That was a mistake on my part.

13:02.099 --> 13:05.039
I should've known there was
no need for such worries.

13:05.097 --> 13:07.064
I hope you can forgive me.

13:15.055 --> 13:17.004
You're just as I expected, Sir Rimuru.

13:17.008 --> 13:21.036
I realized you didn't
intend to ridicule me,

13:21.036 --> 13:23.041
so I was testing you.

13:23.099 --> 13:25.091
But now I know.

13:26.045 --> 13:30.033
That your presence will help Lady Milim
grow and mature as a person.

13:35.017 --> 13:36.009
By the way...

13:37.023 --> 13:39.051
Carrion?

13:39.051 --> 13:40.009
What?

13:40.009 --> 13:42.047
What exactly was so funny again?

13:42.047 --> 13:46.022
Would you explain to me in full detail
in a way I can understand?

13:46.022 --> 13:49.022
H-Hold it! O-Ouch, that hurts!

13:49.022 --> 13:51.052
That hurts! Seriously! I mean it!

13:51.052 --> 13:53.006
Do you see that, Milim?

13:53.006 --> 13:54.098
If you do something bad,
you apologize.

13:54.098 --> 13:57.005
That's the right thing to do.

13:57.005 --> 13:58.065
Yeah, I understand.

13:58.065 --> 14:01.032
And more importantly,
I'll try to not get Frey angry too much.

14:01.032 --> 14:04.066
Hey, don't just chat there and save me!

14:04.066 --> 14:08.041
Hey! Don't ignore me! Ow ow ow ow!

14:09.012 --> 14:10.016
All right, everyone.

14:11.004 --> 14:12.082
The food is ready!

14:18.008 --> 14:20.059
I'm counting on you today.

14:20.094 --> 14:23.063
Middray is a stubborn guy, after all.

14:23.063 --> 14:27.043
So get something tasty that'll
knock his butt on the first bite, okay?

14:28.035 --> 14:30.072
I understand, Lady Milim.

14:31.021 --> 14:33.069
Well then, please enjoy.

14:33.069 --> 14:37.048
Can't say I'm impressed, Lady Milim.

14:37.048 --> 14:43.024
To see them teaching you all
these blasphemous ways.

14:43.009 --> 14:45.057
Blasphemous, as in?

14:45.057 --> 14:48.012
Hmph! To show our gratitude
to our foodstuffs

14:48.012 --> 14:51.037
and enjoy them as is,
in their natural form

14:51.037 --> 14:55.042
has always been the way
we deemed proper since ancient times.

14:55.042 --> 14:57.025
And you presented them like this...

14:57.025 --> 15:00.025
Grilling meat... That much is fine.

15:00.025 --> 15:04.022
But then you stain it
with some mysterious liquid.

15:04.022 --> 15:05.051
Truly deplorable!

15:05.097 --> 15:08.093
What a disrespect for
our natural blessing!

15:08.093 --> 15:12.081
I have no qualms in how you wish
to enjoy them in your domain,

15:12.081 --> 15:17.002
but to involve Lady Milim
in such a custom is outrageous!

15:17.002 --> 15:23.032
I could... I could never accept this!

15:23.032 --> 15:29.087
Milim asked me to make Middray acknowledge
the taste of cooked food...

15:31.053 --> 15:33.063
But seems like it won't be easy.

15:34.025 --> 15:38.042
Rimuru, I didn't know Middray
could be this stubborn.

15:38.085 --> 15:42.013
Should I have him move
to another room for the moment?

15:42.013 --> 15:44.067
I'm sorry for our head priest.

15:44.067 --> 15:47.005
He's not a bad guy, I promise.

15:47.005 --> 15:49.043
I didn't expect he'd be this furious.

15:49.043 --> 15:52.006
Hmm, I thought a taste
would help change his mind,

15:52.006 --> 15:55.035
but seems like I was
taking this too lightly.

15:55.035 --> 15:58.073
I don't want to force him, either,
so I suppose it can't be helped.

16:08.032 --> 16:09.045
What are you do...

16:09.045 --> 16:10.053
Shut up!

16:11.053 --> 16:15.041
See all these ingredients in this soup?

16:16.012 --> 16:19.096
This is the ideal state
that Great Rimuru is striving for.

16:19.096 --> 16:21.092
Huh?
What is she talking about?

16:21.092 --> 16:26.022
Lady Milim has the lycanthropes,
the harpies,

16:26.022 --> 16:28.008
the Majins who once served Clayman,

16:28.008 --> 16:31.072
and Dragonewts like yourself serving her.

16:31.072 --> 16:36.073
Any one of those races alone
possesses tremendous power.

16:37.027 --> 16:42.077
However, if all of you worked together,
you'll gain an even greater power.

16:44.009 --> 16:48.032
You'll understand once you try it.
Please, even just a spoonful.

16:48.032 --> 16:50.011
O-Okay...

16:59.033 --> 17:02.033
Wh-What's this?!

17:02.079 --> 17:05.005
This is called "harmony."

17:05.005 --> 17:08.042
Each individual ingredient
tones itself down

17:08.042 --> 17:11.026
in order to form a complete overall taste.

17:11.008 --> 17:16.022
That's the fervent hope
contained in this soup.

17:16.022 --> 17:18.001
I-I didn't know that.

17:19.006 --> 17:20.077
It's good.

17:20.077 --> 17:23.094
This single spoonful
has so much depth to it,

17:23.094 --> 17:27.007
even better than any vegetable
I've eaten before.

17:27.007 --> 17:29.011
Yeah, of course it would.

17:29.011 --> 17:32.049
Raw veggies versus Shuna's cooking.
It's not even a competition.

17:32.049 --> 17:35.049
Please don't look at us
with those eyes full of pity.

17:36.062 --> 17:38.087
Please remember this:

17:38.087 --> 17:42.005
A cuisine is not complete
with just this one dish.

17:43.000 --> 17:44.092
What do you mean?

17:44.092 --> 17:49.084
If we take this soup as the new nation
that Lady Milim will rule over,

17:49.084 --> 17:52.026
then this loaf of bread is Blumund.

17:52.026 --> 17:55.076
And this steak is
the new kingdom Falmenace.

17:55.076 --> 17:59.001
If this foie gras terrine
is the Dwarven Kingdom,

17:59.001 --> 18:02.014
then this seafood here is
the Sorcerous Dynasty of Thalion.

18:02.059 --> 18:06.052
No cuisine can survive on a single plate.

18:06.052 --> 18:08.096
And the same goes for nations.

18:08.096 --> 18:11.003
By having a broad,
deep connection among them,

18:11.003 --> 18:13.041
you'll get more bountiful
satisfaction out of them.

18:14.057 --> 18:16.041
And that is...

18:17.012 --> 18:19.054
The world that Great Rimuru seeks!

18:20.045 --> 18:22.029
I-It is?

18:22.029 --> 18:25.088
Diplomatic relations
certainly are important.

18:26.038 --> 18:30.046
Even putting the wrong amount of salt
could ruin a dish.

18:30.046 --> 18:35.064
But he's balancing different dishes
together to form a complete full course?

18:35.064 --> 18:39.008
Hmm, I didn't think of it
that deeply, though.

18:39.008 --> 18:40.064
But...

18:40.064 --> 18:42.017
I see!

18:43.048 --> 18:47.086
Also, it takes more than simply
tossing all the ingredients into a pot.

18:47.086 --> 18:49.009
So please take note of that.

18:51.057 --> 18:54.091
Well, now that we've convinced you,

18:54.091 --> 18:57.028
these dishes are best taken
while they're still hot.

18:57.028 --> 19:00.074
Now, everyone.
Please enjoy it before it gets cold.

19:01.054 --> 19:04.004
Digging in!

19:08.079 --> 19:11.055
So tasty!

19:11.055 --> 19:12.092
I see.

19:12.092 --> 19:17.051
Lady Milim was patiently waiting
for me to realize my mistake!

19:17.051 --> 19:22.077
C'mon, Sir Middray, don't be so depressed.
Nobody likes a party pooper.

19:22.077 --> 19:24.048
Let's enjoy it while it's hot!

19:26.006 --> 19:27.048
Hermes!

19:27.048 --> 19:30.082
Uh, what? Why is your head
so red like a melon?

19:32.065 --> 19:34.061
Why so angry, Middray?

19:34.061 --> 19:35.095
Hermes is right.

19:35.095 --> 19:38.099
If you don't dig in now,
I'm gonna chow down all in your stead!

19:39.087 --> 19:42.002
Count yourself lucky, Hermes.

19:42.002 --> 19:48.004
On behalf of Lady Milim and this fine food,
I will forgive this affront!

19:48.004 --> 19:50.004
This one is tasty too, Middray!

19:50.004 --> 19:52.005
So is this one, Lady Milim!

19:52.047 --> 19:55.042
Your sister is really incredible, Benimaru.

19:55.042 --> 19:57.008
I know right?
I'm proud to have her as my sister.

20:00.026 --> 20:02.085
Although unexpected things happened,

20:02.085 --> 20:05.085
the eve of the festival came
to an end without issue...

20:08.006 --> 20:09.047
And finally...

20:10.041 --> 20:12.009
We got to the first day
of the Founder's Festival.

20:22.003 --> 20:24.079
Ladies and gentlemen, I, err...

20:24.079 --> 20:26.091
I am the Demon Lord Rimuru...

20:26.091 --> 20:29.071
No, the almighty Demon Lord Rimuru...

20:33.017 --> 20:35.008
I'm Demon Lord Rimuru.
Nice to meet you.

20:36.055 --> 20:41.064
Today I'm glad you all have answered
my invitation and gathered here today.

20:41.064 --> 20:44.097
I have no intention of being
hostile towards humans.

20:44.097 --> 20:48.056
I'm hoping to build a nation
where everyone can live together in harmony.

20:49.001 --> 20:51.007
Because I believe
that rather than fighting,

20:51.007 --> 20:53.032
monster and human joining hands
and working together

20:53.032 --> 20:56.032
will lead to a better future.

20:56.073 --> 21:01.003
I'm sure some of you are still wary of me.

21:01.003 --> 21:02.082
That's only natural, but...

21:03.028 --> 21:06.041
If you think you can believe in me,
I'd be happy.

21:07.012 --> 21:09.071
You can't build trust overnight.

21:09.071 --> 21:13.071
I believe trust is something we earn by
building it up throughout our relationships,

21:13.071 --> 21:16.005
I'm not going to rush you
to a conclusion on that.

21:17.042 --> 21:20.097
To all the nobles here,
when you return to your homelands,

21:20.097 --> 21:24.001
I want you to be honest and relate
everything you see to your countrymen.

21:24.057 --> 21:28.022
We have already established
friendly relations with several nations.

21:28.022 --> 21:33.083
Even if you don't trust us, I believe those
other nations are worthy of your trust.

21:34.036 --> 21:37.078
If you are biased against me
because I am a slime or a Demon Lord,

21:37.078 --> 21:39.086
I hope that you cast that aside.

21:40.049 --> 21:42.099
I personally have no intention
whatsoever of waging war

21:42.099 --> 21:45.087
simply because someone is
unwilling to join hands with us.

21:45.087 --> 21:50.058
However, if you try to push unequal
treatment on us because we are monsters

21:50.058 --> 21:53.067
or attempt to wage a war
in order to eradicate us...

21:53.067 --> 21:55.029
We'll not show you any mercy.

21:57.008 --> 21:59.097
Well, that's my true feeling.

22:03.068 --> 22:10.018
To all the merchants, adventurers,
and regular peasantry gathered here:

22:10.018 --> 22:13.056
I swear to you that I will not
lay a hand on any of you.

22:13.056 --> 22:16.044
My nation is in need of workers.

22:16.044 --> 22:20.032
If you seek work, I would like all
of you to consider moving here.

22:20.032 --> 22:24.074
As a rule, we guarantee
your right to free expression.

22:24.074 --> 22:29.007
This includes free speech, as well as
the right to choose the job you want.

22:30.002 --> 22:34.071
But of course, you must hold
responsibility for your words and actions.

22:35.042 --> 22:39.055
With all that in mind,
if you're interested in our nation,

22:39.055 --> 22:42.097
then by all means, give some
thought to what I just said.

22:43.055 --> 22:47.085
Going forward, our nation
is planning a multitude of events.

22:48.043 --> 22:53.098
The Tempest Founder's Festival starting
today is only the beginning of that.

22:55.077 --> 23:00.036
Now then, I hope all of you will enjoy
this Tempest Founder's Festival!

24:36.037 --> 24:38.007
Next time,
"The Founder's Festival."
